<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick Middleton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1825–1898</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Frederick Middleton</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Frederick Middleton was a British army officer who commanded the Canadian militia from 1884 to 1890. He led the North-West Field Force against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> in 1885, winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-batoche">Battle of Batoche</a> in May and receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a>'s surrender. He was later forced to resign over the seizure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> belonging to a Métis trader.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-middleton.jpg" alt="Frederick Middleton" width="254" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William James Topley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FrederickMiddleton_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
